  "gaps": [
    "Both pages are JS-rendered (Nuxt SPA); read via a real browser (Playwright). Direct HTTP fetch returns an empty shell.",
    "The testing page describes 3001 as 'La tarjeta fue rechazada' while the errors page says 'The card was declined by the bank'; the errors page wording was used.",
    "HTTP status per code is on the errors page (3001-3005, 3009-3011, 2010 = 402; 2004, 2011 = 422; 2005, 2006 = 400; 2007-2009, 3006, 3012, 32xx = 412) but not encoded above.",
    "No cardholder-name, email or amount rules for sandbox outcomes; no concrete expiry example given.",
    "The 3D Secure flow details for 5454545454545454 (redirect/confirm) are not on the testing page.",
    "Omitted 3201 (merchant not authorized for installments) and account/webhook/storage codes (2001, 2003, 4001, 4002, 600x) as not card-decline related.",
    "retryable true only for 1015/1017 where the message says 'try again later'; 1018 false (retry limit exceeded is our reading); everything else null. Category mapping is our own classification."
  ]
}
